Cuplivo iOS Linux sandbox third-party components
================================================

1. iSH-ARM64 (static libraries libish.a, libish_emu.a, libfakefs.a)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Built at build time (ios/sandbox/build_ish.sh, also run in CI) from the
OpenMinis ish-arm64 fork: https://github.com/OpenMinis/ish-arm64
(pinned revision recorded in build_ish.sh), itself a fork of iSH
(https://github.com/ish-app/ish).

iSH is licensed under the GNU General Public License v3 or later, with
contributions after upstream commit 0e3a4144 additionally licensed under
GPLv2. The additional terms in iSH's LICENSE.IOS also apply; in particular
the iSH copyright holders grant an explicit exception for the conflict
between the GPL and Apple App Store terms of service.

Cuplivo itself is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3,
which is compatible with (and a superset of) the GPLv3 terms above.
Corresponding source for iSH-ARM64 is available from the upstream
repository linked above.

2. Alpine Linux rootfs (resources/alpine-rootfs.zip)
----------------------------------------------------
Generated by tools/ios_rootfs/prepare_alpine_fakefs.py from the official
Alpine Linux minirootfs (https://alpinelinux.org), converted to iSH fakefs
format. Alpine Linux consists of BusyBox (GPLv2), musl libc (MIT) and
Alpine tooling (MIT) among other packages; see Alpine's package pages for
per-package licenses and source locations. The rootfs is used solely as
the guest userland for the optional Linux sandbox feature.
